# OpenShift Vanity Route Automated Failover Configuration Guide

This document provides two distinct, zero-deployment approaches for configuring automated HTTP redirection from **DC2 Cluster 2** to **DC1** on OpenShift Route failures (`502 Bad Gateway`, `503 Service Unavailable`, `504 Gateway Timeout`) for the isolated path (`/uri-2-set/isolation`).

---

## Option 1: Route-Scoped Custom Error ConfigMap (Recommended for Restricted Environments)

Use this option if your cluster security policy blocks `haproxy.router.openshift.io/backend-config-snippet`.

This approach binds a custom HTTP redirect response ConfigMap **exclusively to your specific Route object**. No other routes in your namespace or cluster are affected.

### 1. `configmap.yaml`

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: service-a-redirect-50x-cm
  namespace: service-a-cluster2-ns
data:
  # HAProxy serves this static HTTP response upon encountering 502/503/504 errors
  error-page-50x.http: |
    HTTP/1.1 307 Temporary Redirect
    Location: https://service-my-dc1.abc.net/uri-2-set/isolation
    Content-Type: text/html
    Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate

    <html><body><h1>307 Temporary Redirect</h1><p>Redirecting request to DC1...</p></body></html>

```

### 2. `routes.yaml`

```yaml
# 1. Direct Route for DC2
apiVersion: route.openshift.io/v1
kind: Route
metadata:
  name: service-a-cluster2-direct-route
  namespace: service-a-cluster2-ns
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: service-a
    app.kubernetes.io/component: route
spec:
  host: service-my-dc2.abc.net
  path: /uri-2-set/isolation
  to:
    kind: Service
    name: service-a-cluster2-svc
    weight: 100
  port:
    targetPort: 8080-tcp
  tls:
    termination: edge
    insecureEdgeTerminationPolicy: Redirect
---
# 2. Vanity Route for DC2 (Using Bound ConfigMap)
apiVersion: route.openshift.io/v1
kind: Route
metadata:
  name: service-a-cluster2-vanity-route
  namespace: service-a-cluster2-ns
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: service-a
    app.kubernetes.io/component: route
  annotations:
    haproxy.router.openshift.io/timeout: "10s"
    
    # Enable interception of 502, 503, and 504 errors
    haproxy.router.openshift.io/custom-errors: "502 503 504"
    
    # Binds the custom error response EXCLUSIVELY to this route
    haproxy.router.openshift.io/custom-errors-configmap: "service-a-redirect-50x-cm"
spec:
  host: service-my.abc.net
  path: /uri-2-set/isolation
  to:
    kind: Service
    name: service-a-cluster2-svc
    weight: 100
  port:
    targetPort: 8080-tcp
  tls:
    termination: edge
    insecureEdgeTerminationPolicy: Redirect

```

