## Option 2: Method-Aware Backend Config Snippet (Dynamic HTTP 302 / 307 Redirection)

Use this option if `haproxy.router.openshift.io/backend-config-snippet` is permitted in your cluster.

This approach inspects the incoming HTTP request method directly in HAProxy memory:

* **`POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH` (Uploads / Streams / `InputStream`):** Returns **`HTTP 307 Temporary Redirect`** to ensure the client preserves the original HTTP method and body payload when failing over to DC1.
* **`GET`, `HEAD`, `DELETE`, `OPTIONS` (Standard REST):** Returns **`HTTP 302 Found`**.

### `routes.yaml`

```yaml
# 1. Direct Route for DC2
apiVersion: route.openshift.io/v1
kind: Route
metadata:
  name: service-a-cluster2-direct-route
  namespace: service-a-cluster2-ns
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: service-a
    app.kubernetes.io/component: route
spec:
  host: service-my-dc2.abc.net
  path: /uri-2-set/isolation
  to:
    kind: Service
    name: service-a-cluster2-svc
    weight: 100
  port:
    targetPort: 8080-tcp
  tls:
    termination: edge
    insecureEdgeTerminationPolicy: Redirect
---
# 2. Vanity Route for DC2 (Using HAProxy Snippet)
apiVersion: route.openshift.io/v1
kind: Route
metadata:
  name: service-a-cluster2-vanity-route
  namespace: service-a-cluster2-ns
  labels:
    app.kubernetes.io/name: service-a
    app.kubernetes.io/component: route
  annotations:
    haproxy.router.openshift.io/timeout: "10s"
    
    # HAProxy ACL logic applied strictly to this route's backend block
    haproxy.router.openshift.io/backend-config-snippet: |
      # 1. Match streaming/upload methods (POST, PUT, PATCH)
      acl is_stream_method method POST PUT PATCH

      # 2. Return HTTP 307 for streaming calls to preserve request body payload
      http-response return status 307 default-hdr location "https://service-my-dc1.abc.net%[path]" if { status 502 503 504 } is_stream_method

      # 3. Return HTTP 302 for non-streaming REST calls
      http-response return status 302 default-hdr location "https://service-my-dc1.abc.net%[path]" if { status 502 503 504 } !is_stream_method
spec:
  host: service-my.abc.net
  path: /uri-2-set/isolation
  to:
    kind: Service
    name: service-a-cluster2-svc
    weight: 100
  port:
    targetPort: 8080-tcp
  tls:
    termination: edge
    insecureEdgeTerminationPolicy: Redirect

```

---

## Technical Comparison Matrix

| Property | Option 1: Custom Error ConfigMap | Option 2: Backend Config Snippet |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Route Scope / Isolation** | **100% Isolated** (Bound via route annotation) | **100% Isolated** (Bound to backend stanza) |
| **Impact on Other Routes** | **Zero** | **Zero** |
| **New Deployments Needed** | **None** | **None** |
| **Cluster-Admin Permissions Needed** | **No** | **No** (Unless snippets are globally blocked) |
| **Redirection Behavior** | Fixed **HTTP 307** for all requests | **HTTP 307** for `POST`/`PUT`/`PATCH`; **HTTP 302** for `GET` |
| **`InputStream` Payload Preservation** | Yes | Yes |
